From 6030e9ba66fe3e11b783857af20ba3e83744a3d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 7 Jun 2026 22:25:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 00881/11171] [outer-loop] Truncation guard + gold-control gate
 as first-class metrics (operator directive)

Operator: token truncation is a silent corruptor -- a cut-off solution has no answer and
scores as wrong, dragging accuracy down with NO error/warning. PROVEN here: v1 base 0.30
@256 tok -> 0.633 @512 (66% of GSM8K solutions exceed 256 tokens = two-thirds silently
truncated, garbage result). Fix: _eval now reports truncation_rate + no_answer_rate per
arm; max_new_tokens 768 (headroom above ~320-token solutions); verdict flags
TRUNCATION_INVALID if max_trunc>0.05 and HARNESS_BROKEN if gold<base. v2 (LoRA) showed gold
held at base (harness fixed) but pw dropped -- re-running INSTRUMENTED to confirm it is not
truncation-corrupted before any process-reward conclusion.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
